&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive retention and upsell across our 1K+&amp;nbsp; SMB agencies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retain and grow 7K+ managed advertisers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the operational sales strategy by developing and standardizing operational systems to empower the SMB team to operate at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a high-performing team of sellers to deliver against quarterly revenue targets through effective planning, goal-setting, data analysis, and forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationship with Pinterest’s vendor partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support team strategy for media planning, campaign management, media measurement and media channels (e-commerce, branding, formats and targeting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivate, mentor and develop sales talent (managers and individual contributors), creating a positive culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with internal stakeholders including product, sales operations, and engineering to help Pinterest build a world-class advertising platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish sales team KPIs that allow live time measurement against key quarterly OKRS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, analyze, and communicate key quantitative metrics and business trends as they relate to business health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI utilization: Understand and test various tools &amp;amp; approaches to aid in meeting preparation, performance analysis and ultimately enable prioritize high impact outcomes with velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of professional experience in digital media or online advertising&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-3+ years of sales leadership experience with a demonstrated track record of leading sales teams to exceed quotas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working for or with digital agencies, with a deep knowledge of the agency landscape, key decision makers, operating models, and commercial structures. Proven track record of managing revenue pipeline with forward-looking predictability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to get your hands dirty - from SFDC reporting to call coaching, this leader will need to be able to go deep selectively to help inform the broader strategic vision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven leader with the ability to lead large teams against aggressive goals&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An independent, business-focused creative thinker who is excited to work with customers partners at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, attention to detail, and a bias towards action&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in project management, operations management, and/or vendor management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset &amp;amp; open-mindedness to new techniques, skill development and AI-led workflows to drive success at scale across a diverse set of advertisers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field such as Marketing, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
