&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Accounting Manager I&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Technical Accounting Manager I to join our Technical Accounting and SEC Reporting team. In this role, you’ll research and advise on complex accounting matters, develop accounting policies and support Pinterest’s external reporting. You’ll join a small, highly collaborative team with broad exposure across the business and have opportunities to leverage AI and automation to build scalable accounting processes and internal resources.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently review contracts and analyze complex, material or confidential transactions to establish the appropriate accounting treatment under US GAAP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research technical accounting matters and prepare clear, well-supported accounting memoranda, policies and practical guidance across topics such as leases, share-based compensation, capitalized software, infrastructure and hosting arrangements, long-lived asset impairment, contingencies and restructuring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a technical accounting resource to internal stakeholders, translating complex accounting requirements into practical guidance and providing training to internal teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Accounting Operations, Finance, Legal, Real Estate, and other teams to advise on transactions and resolve accounting matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor new accounting standards and SEC reporting requirements, assess their financial and operational implications and support the implementation of related policies, processes and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI to accelerate research, synthesize accounting guidance and develop scalable internal resources while applying judgment and verification to maintain accuracy, confidentiality and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the preparation and review of financial statements and related disclosures included in Pinterest’s SEC filings, including Forms 10-Q, 10-K and 8-K and the proxy statement&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
