&lt;p&gt;At Pinterest, AI isn&#39;t just a feature, it&#39;s a powerful partner that augments our creativity and amplifies our impact, and we’re looking for candidates who are excited to be a part of that. To get a complete picture of your experience and abilities, we’ll explore your foundational skills and how you collaborate with AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our interview process, what matters most is that you can always explain your approach, showing us not just what you know, but how you think. You can read more about our AI interview philosophy and how we use AI in our recruiting process &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-philosophy-on-ai-in-hiring/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are a leaned-in platform where users come with active intent, not a place to watch funny dance videos or doom scroll through news. As such, we are positioned to succeed in visual search&amp;nbsp; in a differentiated way. As a platform, we are uniquely positioned at the intersection of search, social and commerce. The full-funnel experience across homefeed, search, and related pins - combined with the ability to save, collaborate and curate - enables users to have dynamic, multi-session journeys and go seamlessly from inspiration to action. These journeys are rarely linear and Pinterest enables statefulness better than any other platform - allowing users to stop and start, refine down, broaden out and come back to where they left off - seamlessly navigating between discover, decide and do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a cohesive Search strategy and roadmap in close partnership with Executive, Product, Engineering, Design and other cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build innovative new Search features that tap into the unique user intents on Pinterest. You’ll create products that help users find inspiration, browse products and ultimately find the item they want to buy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and hypothesize opportunities to improve the quality&amp;nbsp; of search experience&amp;nbsp; on Pinterest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with a wide range of disciplines including engineering, data science, design, research, marketing, legal, strategy, and other product managers to define, measure, and drive execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong product sense: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong product sense and ability to collaborate and get buy-in from stakeholders while setting a longer term vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience building AI/ML products: &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrated success in product management or related experience at fast-growing companies particularly working on AI/ML based products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring structure to ambiguity: &lt;/strong&gt;Proven ability to lead in ambiguous environments, aligning across functions, teams, and orgs to deliver on time in a highly collaborative environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expert at weaving together data, user feedback, and intuition: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong analytical skills to define product strategy and drive decision making, making appropriate trade-offs based on data analysis and qualitative feedback from Pinners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in&lt;strong&gt; search is a plus&lt;/strong&gt; but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical strength&lt;/strong&gt;: You’ll partner closely with Engineering teams working with a wide variety of technologies, including Machine Learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field such as computer science or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
