&lt;p&gt;At Pinterest, AI isn&#39;t just a feature, it&#39;s a powerful partner that augments our creativity and amplifies our impact, and we’re looking for candidates who are excited to be a part of that. To get a complete picture of your experience and abilities, we’ll explore your foundational skills and how you collaborate with AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through our interview process, what matters most is that you can always explain your approach, showing us not just what you know, but how you think. You can read more about our AI interview philosophy and how we use AI in our recruiting process &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pinterestcareers.com/our-philosophy-on-ai-in-hiring/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Are you passionate about building and scaling enterprise finance systems that power global business operations? Join Pinterest’s IT Enterprise Systems team, where you’ll play a key role in evolving our Oracle EBS and Finance technology landscape. This is an opportunity to drive meaningful impact by partnering with Finance, Accounting, and cross-functional teams to deliver reliable, scalable, and business-critical ERP solutions that support Pinterest’s continued growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a subject matter expert for Oracle EBS Financials across accounting-centric processes, including General Ledger, Accounts Payable, Cash Management, Fixed Assets, subledger accounting and related integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead solution design, configuration, support, and continuous improvement across accounting processes, with emphasis on close acceleration, data accuracy, control strength, and audit readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI thoughtfully to improve systems analysis, documentation, and operational efficiency, while exercising sound judgment, governance, and risk awareness in finance-critical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support end-to-end integrations between Oracle EBS and external enterprise applications, including SaaS and cloud-based systems that impact accounting operations, reconciliations, and financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Accounting stakeholders to understand operational requirements and translate them into scalable solutions across Oracle EBS and connected cloud platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define and execute the Oracle ERP roadmap in partnership with product owners, systems managers, and business leaders, aligning technology investments with strategic business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess and enhance record-to-report and related finance processes by identifying ways to simplify workflows, strengthen controls, and improve operational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strong SDLC, change management, and SOX-compliant processes across the ERP ecosystem, with a focus on auditability, stability, and risk mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Managed Service Partners and internal teams to promote operational excellence, support best practices, and continuously improve service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Finance and IT to support broader ERP modernization and cloud transformation initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Information Systems, Engineering, Business Systems, Computer Science, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of progressive experience implementing, supporting, and enhancing Oracle EBS in large, complex enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in Oracle EBS Financials, including strong hands-on knowledge of GL, AP, CM, FA, SLA, and accounting control frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Oracle Fusion Cloud Financials is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use AI responsibly in enterprise environments, with attention to security, privacy, governance, and the validation of AI-assisted outputs before use in production or business-critical workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong functional understanding of end-to-end Finance processes, accounting operations, and ERP controls in a public-company or highly regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading Oracle EBS configuration, enhancements, issue resolution, release coordination, and cross-functional systems initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of Oracle EBS integrations, enterprise application architecture, and cloud integration frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of SOX controls, audit readiness, compliance requirements, and change management practices within ERP and financial systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with proven success working across Finance, IT, vendors, and global cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, systems thinking, and a track record of delivering reliable, scalable, and business-focused enterprise solutions.Join us to be part of a forward-thinking team at Pinterest, where your expertise will help lay the foundation for future financial innovation!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
