&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and support scalable enterprise solutions across the Oracle EBS and Finance systems landscape, with a strong focus on technical architecture, integrations, and platform reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior technical expert for Oracle EBS Financials, driving system design, development, customization, troubleshooting, and optimization across key finance workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development and management of integrations between Oracle EBS and internal/external platforms using APIs, middleware, event-driven patterns, and cloud-native integration approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and enhance finance-related services and integration components leveraging AWS and related cloud technologies to improve scalability, resilience, and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development of in-house Oracle MCP and AI-powered components, enabling smarter automation, faster issue analysis, and improved engineering productivity within the fintech domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI thoughtfully as a force multiplier in engineering workflows such as system analysis, documentation, debugging, and automation, while maintaining strong technical judgment and accountability for final outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross-functional engineering teams to translate business requirements into robust technical solutions across Oracle EBS and integration platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive end-to-end technical solution delivery, including architecture, development, testing, deployment, monitoring, and ongoing support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate current finance system architecture and processes, identifying opportunities to modernize integrations, simplify technical workflows, strengthen controls, and improve maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strong software development lifecycle practices, change management, and SOX-compliant controls across enterprise finance applications and integration layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Finance and IT to support broader ERP modernization and cloud transformation initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of progressive experience designing, developing, integrating, and supporting Oracle EBS solutions in large-scale enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience developing Oracle EBS components, integrations using APIs, web services, middleware, and enterprise integration patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or contributing to internal platform capabilities, such as Oracle MCP tools, reusable enterprise components, or AI-enabled engineering tools, is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI-assisted development and enterprise AI use cases, with the ability to validate outputs and apply AI responsibly in regulated, business-critical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical knowledge of SQL, PL/SQL, Oracle APIs, EBS extension frameworks, reporting tools, and related Oracle development technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with middleware and enterprise application architecture, including tools and frameworks such as Oracle SOA Suite, WebLogic, REST APIs, messaging systems, and cloud integration platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with AWS services and cloud-native development, especially for building integration services, automation components, and scalable backend systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead technical initiatives across architecture, design, development, issue resolution, release management, and production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of SOX controls, audit requirements, security, and change management practices within ERP and financial systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, collaboration, and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to work effectively across Finance, IT, platform teams, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving, systems thinking, and engineering judgment, with a track record of delivering secure, scalable, and high-quality enterprise solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join a forward-thinking team where you will help modernize and scale core finance platforms through a combination of Oracle EBS expertise, cloud engineering, API development, and AI innovation. Your work will directly influence how Pinterest builds the next generation of enterprise fintech capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
